    <string name="quick_calc_result_human_years_unit">%1$d HY</string>
    <string name="quick_calc_result_explanation_title">How is this calculated</string>
    <string name="quick_calc_result_explanation_epigenetic">Wang et al. formula (Cell Systems 2020, DOI 10.1016/j.cels.2020.06.006): HY = 16 · ln(age) + 31. Based on DNA methylation — more accurate than the traditional "1 year = 7 years" rule.</string>
    <string name="quick_calc_result_explanation_size_based">AKC/AAHA 2019 table-based method: human-year value is taken from a published table by weight class (Toy / Small / Medium / Large / Giant).</string>
    <string name="quick_calc_result_explanation_aafp">AAHA/AAFP 2021 feline life-stage guidelines: piecewise formula — kitten (15 HY for the first year) + young adult (+9 HY for the second) + 4 HY per additional year. Independent of the Wang method.</string>
    <string name="quick_calc_result_explanation_rabbit">House Rabbit Society + AVMA method: piecewise formula — 30 HY/year up to 4 months, then slowing; from year 1 = 21 HY + 6 HY per additional year. Size only affects expected lifespan.</string>
    <string name="quick_calc_result_explanation_hamster">RVC VetCompass + Animallama method: piecewise formula in months — fast start (1 HY per 4 days), 6 months ≈ 30 HY, then +3–4 HY per month of life.</string>
    <string name="quick_calc_result_explanation_guinea_pig">Oxbow + Animallama method: piecewise formula — weaning ≈ 6 HY, 5 months ≈ 20 HY, then +8 HY/year up to 4 years and +10 HY/year after.</string>
    <string name="quick_calc_result_explanation_rat">Sengupta 2013 method (Int J Prev Med 4(6):624–630): linear formula HY = 13.8 · age + 1.4.</string>
    <string name="quick_calc_result_explanation_mouse">Dutta &amp; Sengupta 2016 method (Life Sciences 152:244–248): piecewise formula — accumulation of human-days across mouse life phases with a decreasing ageing rate.</string>
    <string name="quick_calc_result_explanation_ferret">PMC "Senior Ferret" method (PMC7129291): piecewise formula — +5 HY/month up to six months, 1 year ≈ 40 HY, then +4 HY per additional year.</string>

